ally  redeemed had was he using drugs what was  he doing in his personal life  that could affect his professional uh  career and his professional life and the  editorial pages the columnist and the  editorial page itself were critically  looking at what he could offer  a lot of people in the city and i think  the media  could be  accused of this as well were concerned  about  what would a return of marion barry do  to the city's relationship with congress  which was already kind of frayed from  his previous tenure and did not get much  better under sharon pratt kelly  i wanted to mention a couple names  uh and just have you described for us  mary and barry's relationship with these  people  one name is reverend jesse jackson are  they friends are they foes what's their  relationship i think that at one point  that they were friends  um  one in in 1994 well in 1990 where there  was talk of marion of jesse jackson  running against marion barry there  marion barry made the comment that the  only thing jess is going to do is run  his mouth the only way  so there there is that kind of  competitive uh  relationship that they have they both  were in the movement together but  clearly jesse jackson was much closer to  um to the reverend martin luther king  than than marion barry  at this point i think that there is a  healthy but distant respect for each  other  how about andrew brimmer who is andrew  brimmer what's their relationship andrew  brimmer is the director of the  d.c financial responsibility and  management assistance authority commonly  called the control board here which was  created by congress and  created by congress in march 1995  to actually  help the city to  sort of  work its way out of the financial crisis  much like a control board was created  for new york and a control board created  for philadelphia when those cities  faced  the brink of insolvency and financial  and management crises um and so andrew  bremer is the chairman of that board now  what'